LOCATION: estate

OBJECT: wounds
  GATE: NOT rose_bodies_removed
  LABEL: "Examine the six men"
  THE ROSE GARDEN: "Six men in evening dress, arranged in a half-circle.\n\nWalter knows five of the faces. Judge Wexford. Dr. Fenn. Corliss, the district attorney. Pruitt. Kessler.\n\nThe sixth means nothing to him."
  EXAMINE · JUDGE WEXFORD: "A wound above the bridge of the nose.\nNo powder scorching.\n\nWalter turns the head.\nThere is no exit wound."
  WALTER'S NOTEBOOK: "The other five present the same condition.\n\nNo weapon in any visible hand.\nCause and sequence unestablished.\n\nThe observation is exact. It is the explanation that is missing."
  NOTEBOOK: wounds_note | "Six men in evening dress. A small wound above the bridge of each nose. No corresponding wound behind the skull. No powder marks on the collars."
  EVIDENCE: wounds

OBJECT: watch
  GATE: NOT rose_bodies_removed
  LABEL: "Examine the sixth man's effects"
  THE SIXTH MAN: "No calling card. No monogram. No wallet.\n\nA watch, stopped at 03:17. Its maker's plate has been filed smooth."
  WALTER'S NOTEBOOK: "Unknown male, approximately fifty to sixty.\nClub dress. Identity unrecovered.\n\nAsk the steward. Then the tailor. A blank is still something to investigate."
  NOTEBOOK: watch_note | "The unidentified man's watch is stopped at seventeen minutes past three. The maker's plate has been filed smooth. This alone does not establish the time of death."
  EVIDENCE: watch

OBJECT: knife
  GATE: NOT rose_bodies_removed
  LABEL: "Examine the ground beneath the hedge"
  BENEATH THE HEDGE: "A knife with a butcher's grip. Walter has seen its like in Kessler's shop.\n\nThe blade is too clean for the earth around it."
  EVIDENCE ENVELOPE: "He wraps the handle before lifting it.\n\nLocation recorded. Blade preserved for examination.\nAn object can be useful before it has agreed to explain itself."
  NOTEBOOK: knife_note | "A butcher's knife beneath a hedge root. The blade has been wiped. Its presence is recorded; its use has not been established."
  EVIDENCE: knife

OBJECT: eight
  GATE: NOT birch_bodies_removed AND evidence(naomi) AND object_done(estate, eight)
  LABEL: "Examine the two figures beyond the birches"
  BEYOND THE BIRCHES: "The woman and the boy lie exactly where they were. No one has come for them yet — but Walter no longer has to call her nothing."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Naomi Freeman.\n\nThe boy still has no name on any list Walter has seen."
  WALTER'S NOTEBOOK: "Naomi Freeman, identified. Her son, unidentified male, minor, remains so.\n\nEight people. Two scenes. One investigation — one name closer to whole."
  NOTEBOOK: eight_identified_note | "Naomi Freeman, identified. Her son, unidentified male, minor, remains so.\n\nEight people. Two scenes. One investigation — one name closer to whole."
  EVIDENCE: eight

OBJECT: eight
  GATE: NOT birch_bodies_removed
  LABEL: "Examine the two figures beyond the birches"
  BEYOND THE BIRCHES: "A woman and a boy lie apart from the club members.\n\nSomeone has brought two more sheets. These deaths were not clean. Walter leaves the coverings in place."
  WALTER CORWIN: "No names yet.\n\nThat is a fact about the investigation.\nIt is not a fact about their lives."
  WALTER'S NOTEBOOK: "Unidentified female. Unidentified male, minor.\nRelationship unconfirmed.\n\nEight people. Two scenes. One investigation."
  NOTEBOOK: eight_note | "Six men in the rose garden. A woman and a boy beyond the birches. Eight dead at two adjacent scenes. Their relationship and identities remain unconfirmed."
  EVIDENCE: eight

OBJECT: shoes
  GATE: NOT birch_bodies_removed
  LABEL: "Examine the belongings beside the bodies"
  THE BELONGINGS: "The boy's shoes have been resoled twice.\nThe woman's coat is too light for this hour.\n\nThese are the possessions of people who expected to need them again."
  A POSSIBLE INQUIRY: "Ask at the boardinghouses on Pickman Street.\nSomeone may have given them a room or a meal.\n\nWalter writes it down before the thought can become somebody else's responsibility."
  NOTEBOOK: shoes_note | "The boy's shoes have been resoled. The woman's coat is too light for the season. A boardinghouse inquiry may identify them; clothing cannot establish that nobody will miss them."
  EVIDENCE: shoes

OBJECT: gas
  GATE: NOT topic_done(odell, default)
  TAG: gas_pre_odell
  LABEL: "Examine the terrace windows"
  THE TERRACE WINDOWS: "The heavy leaded casements look out across the terrace toward the garden.\n\nEvery pane is whole. A skim of morning damp clings to the glass, undisturbed."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Nothing broken. The latch is seated from the inside.\n\nWhatever took place in the rose garden began and ended outside."

OBJECT: gas
  GATE: always
  LABEL: "Examine the terrace windows"
  THE TERRACE WINDOWS: "The panes facing the garden are intact.\nWalter runs a finger along the sill. Dust, damp, no soot."
  WALTER'S NOTEBOOK: "No blast damage visible.\nNo burns on the nearest bodies.\n\nIf this was a gas accident, the scene has kept remarkably little of it."
  NOTEBOOK: gas_note | "Windows facing the garden remain intact. Neither the nearby stone nor the clothing shows scorching. The proposed gas accident is unsupported by the visible scene."
  EVIDENCE: gas

OBJECT: register
  GATE: always
  LABEL: "Examine the seating list"
  THE STEWARD'S TABLE: "Five names on the seating list. Six places.\n\nThe last line has not been crossed out. It was never filled."
  WALTER'S NOTEBOOK: "Copy the five names. Preserve the blank.\n\nWEXFORD · FENN · CORLISS\nKESSLER · PRUITT\n\nAn omission is worth keeping in its original shape."
  NOTEBOOK: register_note | "The steward's seating list names Wexford, Fenn, Corliss, Kessler, and Pruitt. A sixth place is set without a name. A missing name is a missing fact, not an explanation."
  EVIDENCE: register